// REGISTRY CONFORMANCE — one format, both readers, and they must never disagree.
//
// Each test runs BOTH readers of `docs/error-codes.txt` over the same bytes in a scratch checkout —
// the build gate, which parses and generates, and `lookup_error_code`, which reads what the gate
// generated — and asserts the safety property: THE TOOL ANSWERS ONLY WHAT THE GATE SANCTIONED, FOR
// THE BYTES ON DISK NOW. `Conformance.maxon` carries the full account of why.
//
// Each of these ran the real bootstrap once, in its own scratch tree under
// `maxon-dev-mcp/test/.maxon/conformance/<name>/` — never a real checkout, because
// `error-codes generate` WRITES into whatever root it is pointed at.

test 'a blank line inside an entry is read the same way by both readers'
	try Conformance.check("blank-line-in-entry")
end 'a blank line inside an entry is read the same way by both readers'

test 'an indented comment is read the same way by both readers'
	try Conformance.check("indented-comment")
end 'an indented comment is read the same way by both readers'

test 'a tab separated key is read the same way by both readers'
	try Conformance.check("tab-separated-key")
end 'a tab separated key is read the same way by both readers'

test 'a duplicate key is rejected by the gate and the tool then refuses'
	try Conformance.check("duplicate-key")
end 'a duplicate key is rejected by the gate and the tool then refuses'

test 'an entry with no doc is rejected by the gate and the tool then refuses'
	try Conformance.check("missing-doc")
end 'an entry with no doc is rejected by the gate and the tool then refuses'

test 'a registry changed under its generated artifact makes the tool refuse'
	try Conformance.check("stale-after-generate")
end 'a registry changed under its generated artifact makes the tool refuse'

// See the note on the same check in `protocol.test.maxon`: a `test` declaration is static, so the
// fixture list is written down twice and this is the check between the copies.
test 'every registry conformance fixture on disk is named by a test in this file'
	try Conformance.requireEveryFixtureHasATest()
end 'every registry conformance fixture on disk is named by a test in this file'
